WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.612
The applied assessment asks you to produce one row per customer with cleaned fields, a quality status,

00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:10.042
and a duplicate rank. Do not overwrite the customer source table.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.082
Build the solution in stages.

00:00:12.082 --> 00:00:13.762
Start with normalization. Add validation.

00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:19.087
Then add duplicate ranking. Finally create the row-level status.

00:00:19.087 --> 00:00:22.747
Run each stage as you build it so errors remain easy to locate.

00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:26.412
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:30.942
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:34.042
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:37.747
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:44.272
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:49.892
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:51.920
not only whether the statement executes.
